{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FixedWidthInteger"},{"text":", with k odd-degree vertices, every distance d between two of them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"satisfies k · (2 · d + 1) ≤ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each distance is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"found.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(k (n + m) log n) for the searches and O(k³) for the matching, with k the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number of odd-degree vertices; O(n + m + k²) memory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The shortest closed walk through every edge at least once (the Chinese postman problem),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by Edmonds and Johnson’s algorithm, or nil when the graph has no edge or its edges are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all connected. Isolated vertices are ignored.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/chinesePostmanTour(weight:)-2g97x"},"references":{"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/PostmanTour":{"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/postmantour","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostmanTour"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/PostmanTour","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"PostmanTour","abstract":[{"text":"A shortest closed walk through every edge at least once: the a